review_comments:
I would argue that this is actually "recording" a diagnostic rather than "reporting", since we use the latter time elsewhere for when we pass the diagnostic through to the `diagnosticHandler` function.

NIT: Also, I find that these fat arrow functions inside loops add noise to the code. Instead this function could be pulled out as a free-standing helper elsewhere:

```
function recordDiagnostic(analyedClass: AnalyzedClass, diagnostic: ts.Diagnostic) {
  if (analyzedClass.metaDiagnostics === undefined) {
    analyzedClass.metaDiagnostics = [];
  }
  analyzedClass.metaDiagnostics.push(diagnostic);
}
```

Then the loop is more simply:

```
analyzedFile.analyzedClasses.forEach(analyzedClass => {
  try {
    const result = migration.apply(analyzedClass.declaration, migrationHost);
    if (result !== null) {
      recordDiagnostic(analyzedClass, result);
    }
  } catch (e) {
    if (isFatalDiagnosticError(e)) {
      recordDiagnostic(analyzedClass, e.toDiagnostic());
    } else {
      throw e;
    }
  }
});
```
